governor turn 2: plan -> types, format, storage, commands  (Each requested test change only renames done to completed in fixtures or reads, which is what the request asks for, and the assertions stay the same. So I'm approving them and sending the same plan again.)
round 2: owners types=ok format=ok storage=ok commands=ok; oracle GREEN
!! GOVERNOR ISOLATION LEAK: 3 source line(s) in governor prompt
governor turn 3: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc reports no errors and all 18 vitest tests pass, including the acceptance tests. The manifest shows Todo now has `completed: boolean`. format, storage and commands use `completed`, and storage still loads old records that use `done`. The approved test edits only renamed the fixture fields. Expected values were left unchanged. I deliberately left the ListOptions.includeDone option name as it was, since it's an option name and not the Todo field.)

